// A var scan of `n` on a molecule that declares `theta` (review finding 24,
// 7 Oct 2026). theta and n are LINKED (theta = n*N, Namics
// Molecule::UpdateVarInfo sets both), and Molecule takes theta over n --
// before the fix every scan step rewrote n while the declared theta held
// all rows at theta = 2 (identical GP, "converged in 0 iterations"). The
// scan now clears the linked key per step and starts from the CONVERTED
// current amount (n = theta/N = 0.1), like Namics' PutVarInfo: rows
// theta 2, 3, 4. Oracle (Namics 3e9eafd, same input + lattice_type +
// output declarations): theta/n identical, GP agrees to 7e-8 relative
// (4.0855459858787e-4 / 6.3494442e-4 / 8.7102172e-4). The .pro numbering
// differs by design (Namics writes the first step as scan_n_linked.pro,
// PySFBox as scan_n_linked_0.pro; REFERENCE.md "File numbering").
lat : flat : geometry : flat
lat : flat : n_layers : 30
lat : flat : lowerbound : surface
lat : flat : upperbound : mirror
lat : flat : lattice_type : simple_cubic
mon : X : freedom : frozen
mon : X : frozen_range : lowerbound
mon : A : freedom : free
mon : W : freedom : free
mon : A : chi_X : -1.0
mol : W : composition : (W)1
mol : W : freedom : solvent
mol : pol : composition : (A)20
mol : pol : freedom : restricted
mol : pol : theta : 2
output : kal : append : false
kal : mol : pol : theta
kal : mol : pol : n
kal : sys : NN : grand_potential
var : mol-pol : scan : n
var : mol-pol : step : 0.05
var : mol-pol : end_value : 0.2
start
